{"type":"standard","title":"Ron Estes","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ron Estes</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q7363747","titles":{"canonical":"Ron_Estes","normalized":"Ron Estes","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Ron Estes</span></span>"},"pageid":30793749,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Ron_Estes%2C_115th_official_photo.jpg/330px-Ron_Estes%2C_115th_official_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":412},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/Ron_Estes%2C_115th_official_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2573,"height":3216},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1374425352","tid":"527909ba-ae40-11f1-98dd-df58d03d3f33","timestamp":"2026-09-12T00:24:31Z","description":"American politician (born 1956)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ron_Estes","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ron_Estes?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ron_Estes?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ron_Estes"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ron_Estes","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Ron_Estes","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ron_Estes?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ron_Estes"}},"extract":"Ronald Gene Estes is an American politician and civil engineer serving as the U.S. representative for Kansas's 4th congressional district since 2017. A member of the Republican Party, he previously served as the 39th Kansas State Treasurer from 2011 until his resignation in 2017 and as treasurer of Sedgwick County from 2004 to 2010.","extract_html":"<p><b>Ronald Gene Estes</b> is an American politician and civil engineer serving as the U.S. representative for Kansas's 4th congressional district since 2017. A member of the Republican Party, he previously served as the 39th Kansas State Treasurer from 2011 until his resignation in 2017 and as treasurer of Sedgwick County from 2004 to 2010.</p>"}